      "name": null,
      "problem": "The recursive formula for the Fibonacci numbers is \n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}={a}_{n+1}+{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}={a}_{2}=1,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nWhat is the eighth number in the sequence?",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting $n=1$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1+2} & ={a}_{1+1}+{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={a}_{2}+{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =1+1 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=2$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2+2} & ={a}_{2+1}+{a}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{4} & ={a}_{3}+{a}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{4} & =2+1 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=3$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3+2} & ={a}_{3+1}+{a}_{3} \\\\ {a}_{5} & ={a}_{4}+{a}_{3} \\\\ {a}_{5} & =3+2 \\\\ {a}_{5} & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=4$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{4+2} & ={a}_{4+1}+{a}_{4} \\\\ {a}_{6} & ={a}_{5}+{a}_{4} \\\\ {a}_{6} & =5+3 \\\\ {a}_{6} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=5$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{5+2} & ={a}_{5+1}+{a}_{5} \\\\ {a}_{7} & ={a}_{6}+{a}_{5} \\\\ {a}_{7} & =8+5 \\\\ {a}_{7} & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=6$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{6+2} & ={a}_{6+1}+{a}_{6} \\\\ {a}_{8} & ={a}_{7}+{a}_{6} \\\\ {a}_{8} & =13+8 \\\\ {a}_{8} & =21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $21$ is the eighth number in the sequence.",
