      "dom_id": "question-214157",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "If\n$f(n+2)=f(n+1)+f(n)$\nwith\n$f(1)=7$ and $f(2)=-2,$\nthen $f(8)=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The recursion relation is\n\n$$\nf(n+2)=f(n+1)+f(n).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=1$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1+2) & =f(1+1)+f(1) \\\\ f(3) & =f(2)+f(1) \\\\ f(3) & =(-2)+7 \\\\ f(3) & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=2$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2+2) & =f(2+1)+f(2) \\\\ f(4) & =f(3)+f(2) \\\\ f(4) & =5+(-2) \\\\ f(4) & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, substituting $n=3,4,5,6$ into the recursive formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(5) & =f(3+2)=f(3+1)+f(3)=f(4)+f(3)=3+5=8, \\\\ f(6) & =f(4+2)=f(4+1)+f(4)=f(5)+f(4)=8+3=11, \\\\ f(7) & =f(5+2)=f(5+1)+f(5)=f(6)+f(5)=11+8=19, \\\\ f(8) & =f(6+2)=f(6+1)+f(6)=f(7)+f(6)=19+11=30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $f(8)=30.$",
